From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:16:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 190/194] glm_moe_dsa: a prompt chunk's second half never
 outgrows its exchange room (ScatterRoom)

wholeDsaHalves (TF_GLM_DSA_HALVES, default on at 3+ ranks) split a chunk of R
rows at RA = R / 2 rounded up to 64 rows and sized each half's reduce-scatter
span by RA's rows. An odd chunk of 128k + 1 rows (R / 2 already a multiple of
64) left the second half R - RA = RA + 1 rows: its exchange needs one more
padded row a rank than the span holds (D 6144: 172,032 bytes at TP4), so
scatterRows returned error.ScatterRoom on every rank at layer 0 and the server
stopped. At TP4 that is a chunk of 2049, 2177, ..., 3969 rows (16 tail
lengths); at TP3 and TP6 the five of them with RA % world == 0 (2305, 2689,
3073, 3457, 3841). A 28,417-id prompt's last chunk is 3,841 rows (soak C2,
chatcmpl-8ff51232): ScatterRoom at TP4.

The first half now rounds the larger half, (R + 1) / 2, up to 64 rows, so the
second is never longer. RA changes only for the lengths that failed (odd R
with R / 2 a multiple of 64); every other chunk splits as before.

scatterRoom/halfRows/halvesFit are the forward's own arithmetic as pure
functions (scatterRows' room check and wholeDsaHalves call them), and
zig build test-glm-halves-host checks every R in 2048..4096 at TP3-TP8
(3 tests: 2 fail before this change, 10/10 pass after).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
